  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Ridbit is given an array a1,a2,…,aNa_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_Na1​,a2​,…,aN​. He needs to find the number of ways to divide the array into contiguous subarrays such that:\n\n\nEach element of the sequence aaa belongs to exactly one of the subarrays.\nThere is an integer mmm such that the MEX of every subarray is equal to mmm. The MEX of a sequence is the smallest non-negative integer which does not occur in this sequence.\nHelp Ridbit with this task.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\leq T \\leq 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤N≤100,0001 \\leq N \\leq 100,0001≤N≤100,000",
      "0≤ai≤N0 \\leq a_i \\leq N0≤ai​≤N for each valid iii"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers a1,a2,…,aNa_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_Na1​,a2​,…,aN​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer ― the number of ways to divide the sequence, modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n6\n1 0 0 1 0 1\n3\n1 2 3",
        "output": "5\n4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: The five valid ways to divide the sequence are:\n\n[1,0,0,1,0,1][1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1][1,0,0,1,0,1]\n[1,0],[0,1,0,1][1, 0], [0, 1, 0, 1][1,0],[0,1,0,1]\n[1,0,0],[1,0,1][1, 0, 0], [1, 0, 1][1,0,0],[1,0,1]\n[1,0,0,1],[0,1][1, 0, 0, 1], [0, 1][1,0,0,1],[0,1]\n[1,0],[0,1],[0,1][1, 0], [0, 1], [0, 1][1,0],[0,1],[0,1]"
      }
    ]
  },
